    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1300">

                <pb facs="1034" n="918" sameAs="frus:frus1912/pg918"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.00/3534.</note>
                <head ana="#head_untitled-inferred-from-preceding-sibling-head">[Untitled]</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Embassy</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Mexico</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1912-04-08T21:00:00-06:36">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">April 8, 1912—9 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>As the Mexican National Railway refused to grant any of the demands of the
                    American employees, these, amounting to from 700 to <pb facs="1035" n="919"
                        xml:id="pg919"/> 800, will strike on the 15th and leave their posts. I have
                    used all my influence with the Government, the railways, and the men to prevent
                    the crisis and am deeply disappointed that no good result has followed.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Wilson.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
